{"chunk_id": "dc85fa3ada42", "text": "In heaven, the apsara Urvasi confesses her desire for Arjuna, saying she has long been drawn to his virtues. Arjuna, embarrassed and resolute, refuses her advances, explaining that he regards her as a mother because she was connected with the ancient ancestors of his lineage. Urvasi insists that apsaras are free in love, but Arjuna continues to treat her with reverence and declines. Enraged at being rejected, she curses him to live among women as a eunuch and dancer. Arjuna later reports the event to Chitrasena, and Indra reassures him that the curse will ultimately help him during the Pandavas\u2019 future year of hiding. The passage highlights Arjuna\u2019s restraint and reframes the curse as a strategic blessing.\nArjuna respectfully rejects Urvasi\u2019s advances, is cursed to become a eunuch, and Indra explains the curse will aid him during the Pandavas\u2019 future incognito exile.\nThemes: self-control, curse as destiny, divine lineage, sexual ethics, future exile foreshadowing", "vector": [0.008545726537704468, -0.024033553898334503, -0.008878947235643864, 0.012683218345046043, 0.01067695114761591, 0.019118545576930046, -0.016716578975319862, -0.002568577416241169, -0.006574169732630253, -0.031461600214242935, 0.010066046379506588, 0.01233611349016428, 0.02320050075650215, -0.008038952946662903, -0.019451767206192017, 0.009816130623221397, 0.052982114255428314, 0.009961915202438831, 0.025671890005469322, -0.016910959035158157, -0.008726220577955246, -0.01549476943910122, -0.006178469862788916, -0.008156968280673027, -0.03429397940635681, 0.024366775527596474, 0.00248527224175632, -0.03726520016789436, -0.0038320396561175585, -0.013953623361885548, -0.03132275864481926, 0.0019819699227809906, -0.002129489555954933, -0.02146497555077076, -0.03829262778162956, 0.002896591555327177, -0.009670346975326538, -0.02156216651201248, 0.030934002250432968, 0.007657137233763933, 0.0006247890996746719, -0.008844236843287945, -0.027060